ianek wrote:
> I wonder if Lojban permits lujvo to be composed only from cmavo. Lujvo
> are brivla, so things like pavroi shouldn't work.

It works, at would be roughly similar to using the English word "once" 
as an adjective (e.g. "once-used")

> But some cmavo
> contructs work as selbri, so rolmoi and nunrolmoi and such should
> work, no?

Yes.

In most cases, cmavo-compounds would be used in their non-lujvo form, 
paroi, romoi.  But if you have a reason to treat them as a selbri, you can.

Sometimes meaning could be tough to determine of course.  roirmoi 
doesn't make much sense.

